The relevant lines of code are in extralev.c:

        if (rn2(2)) {
                ghostobj = mksobj_at(FAKE_AMULET_OF_YENDOR, x, y,
TRUE, FALSE);
                ghostobj->known = TRUE;
        }

where the identification is done with ghostobj->known = TRUE;

This code block has been unchanged since v3.1.0 (thanks to Ali's
Nethack Source page for all the historical sources), except that
mksobj_at now takes a 5th parameter, an is_artifact flag, which for
fake amulets is set to false.

In v3.0.0 (3.0.e), the relevant code block is

	if (rn2(2)) {
		ghostobj = mksobj_at(AMULET_OF_YENDOR,x,y);
		ghostobj->spe = -1;
		ghostobj->known = TRUE;
	}
which still contains ghostobj->known = TRUE;

The next oldest release I found was 2.3, which didn't have a rogue
level at all, and hence no extralev.c.  So, let's just say, that's the
way it's always been.

I'm not sure how to explain your wizmode testing, though... the
relevant code has been unchanged for time immemorial!  I don't think
there is any chance a random amulet is created in the ghost pile, but
are you absolutely sure it was a fake AOY? and unidentified?

To be sure, I did a wizmode test for every class in 3.4.2, and each
one found no amulet, or a pre-identified fake.  A diff of extralev.c
for 3.4.0 and 3.4.2 showed them to be exactly the same.

